1
00:00:00,350 --> 00:00:02,622
Three charts. Three new skills to test.

2
00:00:02,991 --> 00:00:04,799
Squeezes, support and targets.

3
00:00:05,299 --> 00:00:08,245
Question one. The Bollinger Bands have squeezed tight.

4
00:00:08,593 --> 00:00:11,273
Which way will it break: up, down, or can't tell?

5
00:00:15,123 --> 00:00:16,846
Trick question. You couldn't tell.

6
00:00:17,254 --> 00:00:23,855
A squeeze says a bigger move is coming, but not which way. This time it broke down. Wait for the break, then decide.

7
00:00:24,355 --> 00:00:27,715
Question two. Price is testing support for the third time.

8
00:00:28,053 --> 00:00:29,078
Bounce, or break?

9
00:00:32,928 --> 00:00:33,619
It broke.

10
00:00:34,013 --> 00:00:39,414
Each pullback was shallower, and volume picked up on the push. But no level breaks every time.

11
00:00:39,928 --> 00:00:42,819
Question three. You bought near the bottom of the range.

12
00:00:43,193 --> 00:00:45,899
Where does your take-profit go? A, B, or C?

13
00:00:49,749 --> 00:00:51,773
A, just below the old resistance.

14
00:00:52,110 --> 00:00:58,460
C cuts a good trade short, and B sits beyond a level that's turned price away before, so it may never fill.

15
00:00:58,960 --> 00:01:01,704
How many did you get? Tell me your score in the comments.

16
00:01:02,095 --> 00:01:05,727
Practise on real charts from the game, at memestreet.net.

